        "content": "{\"complete_source\": \"After brushing your teeth, apply a small amount of natural aloe vera gel directly to the inflamed gums.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to soothe mouth sore caused from biting gums\\\"} It can also be used to cure viral oral lesions, ulcers, and gum abscesses.  Aloe vera can be directly applied to red and inflamed gum tissues. Swish the tea around your mouth to sooth your gums before swallowing.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:Apply aloe vera on sore gums. Allow to to steep for five minutes and cool slightly before drinking. Put one tea bag of chamomile in a cup of boiling water. Do this three times a day for five days.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:Soothe sore gums with chamomile tea. Use a q-tip to apply a small amount of 100% pure honey to sore areas inside your mouth. It can be used to treat sore gums, ulcers and other problems inside the mouth. {\\\"passages\\\":\\\"passage 1:1 Honey can produce hydrogen peroxide and kill bacteria by dehydrating it.\", \"original_answer\": \"Three methods can be used to soothe a mouth sore from biting gums. First, you can apply a small amount of 100% pure honey to the sore area three times a day for five days using a q-tip. Honey has antibacterial properties that can help treat sore gums and ulcers. Second, you can drink chamomile tea. After steeping the tea for five minutes, cool it slightly and swish it around your mouth before swallowing. Finally, you can apply aloe vera gel directly to the inflamed gum after brushing your teeth. Aloe vera can help cure inflamed gum tissues, oral lesions, and gum abscesses.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}",
